12. The named character references of the WHATWG HTML Living Standard
===============================================================================

What: the table of HTML's named character references (the names, such as "&amp;" and "&lt",
and the characters they stand for), from the WHATWG HTML Living Standard
(https://html.spec.whatwg.org/, section "Named character references"; the file
https://html.spec.whatwg.org/entities.json, taken on 2026-11-23). LOSAT Web's results screen
decodes them where it shows the text of a report written with -html, as a browser shows it.
Files (from the repository's root, outside the losat crate):
web/app/src/domain/html-named-references.ts, written from that file by
web/app/scripts/html-named-references.mjs.
License: the standard is under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License;
WHATWG's statement: "To the extent portions of it are incorporated into source code, such
portions in the source code are licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License instead." WHATWG
generates entities.json in the repository https://github.com/whatwg/html-build (the directory
entities/, where it is checked in as entities/out/entities.json), whose LICENSE file has the
same text. The license:

